<reactions>
<!-- 
	//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
	// Reaction System													//
	//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
	The reaction system can be used to execute effects when certain
	conditions are met.
	Take note that the triggers are NOT persisted, which means you should
	refrain from using delta triggers. Check the runtime documentation to
	find out which triggers are instant triggers or delta triggers:
	http://127.0.0.1:8080/GameServer/docs.jsp
	
	The initial use-case is "ConditionalBuffs":
	A specific zone buff is started when a set of other zone buffs
	are active at the same time.
	Vice-versa that buff will also be cancelled by an inverted condition.
	
	!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
	!! WARNING: This system makes it possible to created endless loops  !!
	!!          Make extra sure your triggers result in a "false"		!!
	!!          after executing the reaction effects!					!!
	!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	Cascaded trigger lists for boolean AND/OR
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	The list of triggers works as in any other place of the game as a
	boolean "AND", which means all triggers have to be fulfilled.
	To achieve a boolean "OR" you can specify another trigger list instead
	of a single trigger, encapsulated in a <any> tag. Example:
	<triggers>   										<- all have to trigger
		<zonebuffactive name="buffA" amount="1"/>
		<any>											<- only one has to trigger
			<zonebuffactive name="buffB" amount="0"/>
			<zonebuffactive name="buffC" amount="0"/>
		</any>
	</triggers>
	In this example the effects will be executed when buffA is active
	and either buffB or buffC is missing.

	You can make this even more complex using the <all> tag, which acts as
	a boolean "AND" like the trigger list itself:
	<triggers>   										<- all have to trigger
		<zonebuffactive name="buffA" amount="1"/>
		<any>											<- only one has to trigger
			<zonebuffactive name="buffB" amount="0"/>
			<all>										<- all have to trigger
				<zonebuffactive name="buffC" amount="0"/>
				<zonebuffactive name="buffD" amount="0"/>
			</all>
		</any>
	</triggers>
	This example triggers when Either buffB is active together with buffA,
	or when buffA, buffC and buffD are active at the same time.
	
	Hint:
	<triggers> is always the same as <all>
	So instead of <triggers><all>...</all></triggers>
	just use <triggers>...</triggers>
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	
	
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	Inverted triggers, or NOT-triggers
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	Some triggers cannot be inverted with just the regular properties.
	For example:
	Trigger when the user has any amount of Planks *except* when he as 500
	To achieve such a trigger you can invert the trigger like this:
	<resource item="Planks" min="500" max="500" invert="true />
	The invert=true attribute will invert the logic of this trigger,
	so it will not trigger for 500 Planks, but for any other amount it will.
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	
	//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
-->

	<!-- Valentine Population -->
	<reaction name="ReactionStart_ValentineSpeedUpPopulationGrowthZoneConditional">
		<triggers>
			<eventrunning name="Valentines2019plus_Content"/>
			<zonebuffactive name="SpeedUpPopulationGrowthValentineZoneConditional" amount="0"/>
			<buffactive name="EffectBuffFlowerBouquet" min="5"/>
		</triggers>
		<effects>
			<applyzonebuff name="SpeedUpPopulationGrowthValentineZoneConditional"/>
		</effects>
	</reaction>
	
	<reaction name="ReactionStop_ValentineSpeedUpPopulationGrowthZoneConditional">
		<triggers>
			<zonebuffactive name="SpeedUpPopulationGrowthValentineZoneConditional" amount="1"/>
			<buffactive name="EffectBuffFlowerBouquet" max="4"/>
		</triggers>
		<effects>
			<cancelzonebuff name="SpeedUpPopulationGrowthValentineZoneConditional"/>
		</effects>
	</reaction>
	
	
